  "worked_solution": "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $a∥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are parallel, and\n\n- $a⊥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are perpendicular.\n\nIn the given diagram, there are two pairs of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $q$ is perpendicular to $r,$ which we write as $q⊥r$\n\n- $q$ is perpendicular to $s,$ which we write as $q⊥s.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14128162/assets/063ecc105da75d9ba1b3c242476f1353dec82ca9ec13df48f4f480f5f490cb94.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct statement is $q⊥r$ and $q⊥s.$",
